FileCat AppImage runtime: corresponding source
==============================================

FileCat's Linux AppImage (FileCat-<version>-x86_64.AppImage) begins with the
AppImage type2-runtime, the small static program that mounts the application
payload and starts FileCat. That runtime is statically linked with libfuse
3.15.0, which is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 (LGPL-2.1). This archive is published with every FileCat AppImage
release. It carries the complete source of the runtime, including libfuse and
the change applied to it, and a script that rebuilds the runtime and relinks it
with a modified libfuse, for the source and relinking terms of LGPL-2.1
section 6.


1. The runtime these sources correspond to
------------------------------------------

  file       runtime-x86_64 (AppImage type2-runtime, x86_64, static PIE)
  bytes      944632
  SHA-256    617aa77314d57c8b8e4fae9c3f0b35af7b30d5529cb69e98f64f92510ed98a46
  source     https://github.com/AppImage/type2-runtime
             commit fedfad51acc2860b2916a1eef32ba4a500ff31ef
  published  GitHub release asset 657374641 (runtime-x86_64 of the upstream
             "continuous" release, 2026-10-19T20:37:12Z), built by upstream
             GitHub Actions run 39320578745, job 118293253809, and signed
             there with key 570C77ACEA40C0F1B758902CBF96CCA56490F695

FileCat keeps these exact bytes in its own repository and builds every
AppImage from them. appimagetool changes one thing when it assembles the
AppImage: it writes a 16-byte MD5 digest into the runtime's .digest_md5
section at offset 932096. To check that an AppImage starts with this runtime:

  head -c 944632 FileCat-<version>-x86_64.AppImage > runtime-prefix
  dd if=/dev/zero of=runtime-prefix bs=1 seek=932096 count=16 conv=notrunc
  sha256sum runtime-prefix        # 617aa77314d57c8b...


2. Contents
-----------

  sources/fuse-3.15.0.tar.xz
      libfuse 3.15.0 release tarball as published at
      https://github.com/libfuse/libfuse/releases/download/fuse-3.15.0/fuse-3.15.0.tar.xz
      SHA-256 70589cfd5e1cff7ccd6ac91c86c01be340b227285c5e200baa284e401eea2ca0
      The library is LGPL-2.1 (LGPL2.txt); the utilities, which the runtime
      does not contain, are GPL-2.0 (GPL2.txt).

  sources/squashfuse-0.5.2.tar.gz
      squashfuse 0.5.2, https://github.com/vasi/squashfuse/archive/0.5.2.tar.gz
      SHA-256 db0238c5981dabbd80ee09ae15387f390091668ca060a7bc38047912491443d3
      BSD-2-Clause.

  sources/type2-runtime-fedfad51acc2860b2916a1eef32ba4a500ff31ef.tar.gz
      https://github.com/AppImage/type2-runtime/archive/fedfad51acc2860b2916a1eef32ba4a500ff31ef.tar.gz
      SHA-256 e27ea3c837e9c660e1a9a2993b673ae93bbb53077330efba8654031e302d4e8e
      MIT. runtime.c, its Makefile and linker script, the upstream build
      scripts, and patches/libfuse/mount.c.diff, the change applied to
      libfuse (fusermount is taken from $FUSERMOUNT_PROG).

  producer-packages.txt
      The 138 Alpine packages, with versions, that the upstream build
      installed or upgraded in its base image, taken from the apk lines of
      the job log of run 39320578745, job 118293253809.

  rebuild.sh
      Rebuilds the runtime in that environment, and relinks a FileCat
      AppImage with a rebuilt runtime.

  SHA256SUMS
      Checksums of the other files in this archive (sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS).

The runtime also contains static code from four Alpine packages: musl 1.2.5
(musl-dev 1.2.5-r11, MIT), zstd 1.5.6 (zstd-static 1.5.6-r2, BSD-3-Clause
or GPL-2.0), zlib 1.3.2 (zlib-static 1.3.2-r1, Zlib) and mimalloc 2.1.7
(mimalloc2-dev 2.1.7-r0, MIT). Their license texts are in the AppImage under
usr/lib/filecat/licenses/appimage-runtime. Their sources are available from
Alpine (https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports) and from their projects.


3. How upstream built the runtime
---------------------------------

The upstream workflow .github/workflows/build.yaml ran
scripts/docker/build-with-docker.sh for x86_64 on an ubuntu-24.04 runner:

  a. Base image: alpine:3.21, which the job resolved to
     docker.io/library/alpine:3.21@sha256:ce64758a109eb420d874a118f87920e625e12d3634e03b4a5573fd9f6e5d3507
  b. scripts/docker/Dockerfile installed the build packages:
       apk add --no-cache bash alpine-sdk util-linux strace file autoconf
         automake libtool xz eudev-dev gettext-dev linux-headers meson
         zstd-dev zstd-static zlib-dev zlib-static clang musl-dev mimalloc-dev
     Among them: clang19 19.1.4-r0, gcc 14.2.0-r4, binutils 2.43.1-r3,
     meson 1.6.1-r0, samurai 1.2-r6, autoconf 2.72-r0, automake 1.17-r0,
     libtool 2.4.7-r3, musl-dev 1.2.5-r11, mimalloc2-dev 2.1.7-r0,
     zlib-static 1.3.2-r1 and zstd-static 1.5.6-r2 (all: producer-packages.txt).
  c. scripts/common/install-dependencies.sh downloaded libfuse 3.15.0 and
     squashfuse 0.5.2, checked the SHA-256 values above, applied
     patches/libfuse/mount.c.diff to libfuse, built libfuse as a static
     library with meson and ninja, and built squashfuse with autotools
     (LDFLAGS=-static), installing both into the image. Compiler flags map
     the temporary build directory to "." so it does not reach the binary.
  d. The workflow wrote src/runtime/version:
       https://github.com/AppImage/type2-runtime/commit/fedfad5
  e. scripts/build-runtime.sh compiled src/runtime/runtime.c with clang and
     linked it as a static PIE against squashfuse, squashfuse_ll, zstd, zlib,
     fuse3 (libfuse), mimalloc and musl. It then moved the debug information
     to runtime-x86_64.debug, stripped the binary, added a .gnu_debuglink
     section and wrote the AppImage magic bytes "AI\x02" at offset 8.


4. Rebuilding the runtime
-------------------------

Requirements: Linux on x86_64 (or Docker/Podman emulation of linux/amd64),
Docker or Podman, bash, GNU coreutils and network access to Docker Hub and
the Alpine package mirror; --unpack-libfuse also needs tar, xz and patch.
The libfuse, squashfuse and type2-runtime sources come from this archive;
only the base image and the Alpine packages are downloaded.

  ./rebuild.sh

writes out/runtime-x86_64 and out/runtime-x86_64.debug and reports whether
the new runtime is byte-identical to the one above. It checks the sources
against SHA256SUMS, starts the pinned base image, installs the packages of
step 3b, and repeats steps 3c to 3e inside the container. Step 3c is the
upstream script with its two downloads replaced by the archives in sources/
(and a placeholder /dev/fuse, so that libfuse's install step does not need
to create a device node); step 3e runs scripts/build-runtime.sh from the
type2-runtime source unchanged. CONTAINER_ENGINE=podman selects Podman when
both are installed.

Alpine keeps only the current version of each package in its repositories,
so a later rebuild installs the then-current Alpine 3.21 packages; by
2026-10-29 musl-dev 1.2.5-r11 had become 1.2.5-r12. rebuild.sh lists every
producer package whose version it could not install
(out/package-differences.txt). Different package versions can give a runtime
that works the same but differs in its bytes. When FileCat prepared this
archive, on 2026-10-29, ./rebuild.sh with Podman 4.9.3 reproduced the runtime
byte for byte, with musl-dev 1.2.5-r12 and seven other packages newer than
the producer's.

  ./rebuild.sh --expect-shipped

fails (exit status 3) unless the rebuilt runtime is identical.


5. Relinking FileCat with a modified libfuse
--------------------------------------------

  ./rebuild.sh --unpack-libfuse ./libfuse
      Unpacks libfuse 3.15.0 into ./libfuse with the type2-runtime patch
      applied. Change it as you like.

  LIBFUSE_DIR=./libfuse ./rebuild.sh --out ./out-modified
      Builds the runtime as in section 4, with that libfuse tree in place of
      the bundled release (the tree must not contain a build directory).

  ./rebuild.sh --relink FileCat-<version>-x86_64.AppImage \
        ./out-modified/runtime-x86_64 FileCat-relinked-x86_64.AppImage
      Writes a new AppImage: the new runtime followed by FileCat's unchanged
      payload (the squashfs image that starts right after the old runtime).

The runtime finds its payload where its own ELF image ends, so a runtime of
any size works. The relinked file has a zeroed .digest_md5 section and no
signature; neither is needed to run it. Run it as before, for example
./FileCat-relinked-x86_64.AppImage --version, or with
APPIMAGE_EXTRACT_AND_RUN=1 on systems without FUSE.

Instead of --relink, appimagetool --runtime-file ./out-modified/runtime-x86_64
can assemble a new AppImage from an AppDir;
FileCat-<version>-x86_64.AppImage --appimage-extract unpacks FileCat's AppDir
into squashfs-root.
